+# OUTLAW CITY: N4 Stage B readiness (PLAN ONLY) and the Device Simulator test
+
+**Status:** PLAN AWAITING ARCHITECT REVIEW. No Studio edits; no sign built.
+
+**Stage B is blocked until all four hold:**
+1. The owner authorizes it.
+2. The Architect reviews this plan.
+3. The four current signs pass the phone-simulator readability check in section 4.
+4. Owner navigation feedback is obtained (rollout gate item 6).
+
+**Source of the measurements:** the read-only Studio inspection recorded at `6031627` (`docs/audits/2026-10-16_n4-rollout-readiness/TEST_EVIDENCE.md`).
+- Nothing near these junctions has changed since then. Stage A's three signs are at the plaza ring, 180+ studs away.
+- **A fresh re-check could not be run for this plan:** no Studio instance was connected to my tools at the time (`list_roblox_studios` returned none). The re-check is listed as the first implementation step (section 3).
+
+**Boundaries:**
+- No other signs, renaming, roads or gameplay changes.
+- Pursuit 130 / 100 / 0.25 / 8; one police unit; siren off; anti-cheat monitor-only; no external assets.
+- Multiplayer is MULTIPLAYER UNVERIFIED.
+
+## 1. The two junctions
+Both are 4-arm junctions on 1st St (z = −300). Their north arm is the connector road to the highway, so these are the first junctions a driver meets coming off the highway, and the last before getting onto it.
+
+### (100, −300): "1st St" / "C Ave"
+| Corner | Post | Sidewalk | Road / marking / nearest solid | Approach scores (N S W E, out of 4) | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **(+,+)** | **(122, −278)** | Block_3_1 (all 3 parts) | 3.80 / 4.84 / 62.99 (Building_2_1_2) | **N4 S3 W4 E1** | **Proposed.** Weak approach E (from the grid edge); the highway connector (N) scores 4/4 |
+| (−,+) | (78, −278) | Block_2_1 | 3.80 / 4.84 / 15.73 | N4 S1 W3 E4 | Valid, but weak on S (traffic from the plaza ring heading to the highway). Not chosen |
+| (+,−), (−,−) | (122, −322), (78, −322) | none (off grid) | — | — | Rejected |
+
+### (−100, −300): "1st St" / "B Ave"
+| Corner | Post | Sidewalk | Road / marking / nearest solid | Approach scores | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **(+,+)** | **(−78, −278)** | Block_2_1 | 3.80 / 4.84 / 60.68 (Building_1_1_2) | **N4 S3 W4 E1** | **Proposed.** Weak approach E (the 200-stud link from the (100, −300) junction, which is itself signed) |
+| (−,+) | (−122, −278) | Block_1_1 | 3.80 / 4.84 / 15.90 | N4 S1 W3 E4 | Valid, but weak on S (plaza-ring traffic). Not chosen |
+| (+,−), (−,−) | (−78, −322), (−122, −322) | none (off grid) | — | — | Rejected |
+
+**Why both use corner (+,+):**
+- Both highway connector approaches (N) and both plaza-ring approaches (S) score 3–4.
+- No fitting corner puts the weak approach on the west perimeter at (−100, −300): the only corners with a weak west approach are off-grid.
+- The scores are the geometric planning screen. Rendered views are the acceptance evidence (section 3).
+
+## 2. Geometry, labels, counts
+- **Design:** the approved design unchanged.
+  - Post 0.4 × 10.4 × 0.4.
+  - Blades 7 × 1.5 × 0.2, cantilevered away from the junction (+X and +Z from a (+,+) corner).
+  - 4 SurfaceGuis per sign (GothamBold, PPS 50, LightInfluence 0, MaxDistance 150).
+  - Atomic model; all parts anchored with CanCollide, CanQuery, CanTouch and CastShadow false.
+- **Blade footprints:**
+
+  | Sign | Blade_EW centre | Blade_NS centre |
+  |---|---|---|
+  | (100, −300) | (125.7, 8.6, −278), x 122.2..129.2 | (122, 10.2, −274.3), z −277.8..−270.8 |
+  | (−100, −300) | (−74.3, 8.6, −278), x −77.8..−70.8 | (−78, 10.2, −274.3), z −277.8..−270.8 |
+
+  These are all on the stated block, 3.9 studs from the road.
+- **Labels** (plain names, as approved so far):
+  - `StreetSign_100_-300` = "1st St" / "C Ave";
+  - `StreetSign_-100_-300` = "1st St" / "B Ave".
+
+  Themed names remain an open owner choice; choosing them would rename all signs in a separate approved change.
+- **Counts after Stage B:**
+  - 6 signs;
+  - BaseParts 328 → **334**;
+  - colliding **114**;
+  - sign SurfaceGuis 16 → **24**.
+
+## 3. Implementation steps (when unblocked)
+1. **Backup** (owner, verified in the Studio log), then a read-only re-check of the two corners in the current place, repeating section 1.
+2. **Data:** add two entries to `CityLayout.STREET_SIGNS`: `{X=100, Z=-300, CornerX=22, CornerZ=22}` and `{X=-100, Z=-300, CornerX=22, CornerZ=22}`.
+3. **Spec:** extend the existing street-sign tests: count 6, expected names, exact posts. All the per-sign checks already loop over every sign.
+4. **Studio:** `buildStreetSigns` adds only the two missing models; the existing four are skipped by name.
+5. **Verify:**
+   - 334 / 114, 24 sign GUIs;
+   - City `6527bae1`, stop-line `f958ecfa`, buildings `8b66ade9` and prototype `87d79268` unchanged;
+   - the Stage A signature `18eef2d0` unchanged;
+   - footprints and clearances read from the place;
+   - all tests pass.
+6. **Evidence:**
+   - rendered views from all 4 incoming approaches of each junction at 30 and 60 studs, including from the highway connector;
+   - no hidden letters;
+   - drive past and walk through (no bump or touch);
+   - police, jail, robbery, vehicle and dealership regressions;
+   - 3 + 3 FPS and memory runs before and after;
+   - duplicate checks (restart, repeated builder calls, rebuild).
+7. **Rollback:** remove the two entries, delete `StreetSign_100_-300` and `StreetSign_-100_-300`, and restore the spec. It must return exactly 328 / 114, 16 sign GUIs, the four signs with signatures `87d79268` and `18eef2d0`, and 216 tests.
+
+## 4. Device Simulator test for the four existing signs (short, targeted)
+**Who:** I can't switch on Studio's Device Simulator myself.
+1. The owner clicks **Test → Device** in Studio (Device Simulator) and picks **iPhone 7 (667 × 375, landscape)**.
+2. The owner starts Play and tells me.
+3. Then I drive the camera and take the captures.
+4. Repeat with one larger phone (e.g. iPhone 14 Pro Max, landscape).
+
+**Views:** for each of the four signs, the two strongest approaches at 30 and 60 studs, from the same positions as the desktop evidence. Driver eye at y 5 in the incoming lane, aimed at the cross-street blade.
+
+| Sign | Approach A (30, 60) | Approach B (30, 60) |
+|---|---|---|
+| (100, 100) 3rd St / C Ave | from N: (91.2, 5, 70) / (91.2, 5, 40) → "3rd St" | from W: (70, 5, 108.8) / (40, 5, 108.8) → "C Ave" |
+| (−100, −100) 2nd St / B Ave | from N: (−108.8, 5, −130) / (−108.8, 5, −160) → "2nd St" | from E: (−70, 5, −108.8) / (−40, 5, −108.8) → "B Ave" |
+| (100, −100) 2nd St / C Ave | from S: (108.8, 5, −70) / (108.8, 5, −40) → "2nd St" | from W: (70, 5, −91.2) / (40, 5, −91.2) → "C Ave" |
+| (−100, 100) 3rd St / B Ave | from N: (−108.8, 5, 70) / (−108.8, 5, 40) → "3rd St" | from E: (−70, 5, 91.2) / (−40, 5, 91.2) → "B Ave" |
+
+That is 16 captures per device. Each is taken twice; the second is kept, because the first after a camera jump can miss SurfaceGui text.
+
+**Also record:**
+- whether the HUD (touch controls, Spawn Car button, cash) covers the sign in any view;
+- idle FPS facing the plaza ring for 10 s per device (simulator FPS is indicative only, not a real-phone measurement).
+
+**Pass (provisional, per the Architect):**
+- **30 studs:** every name fully legible on both devices, with no letter clipped and no HUD overlap.
+- **60 studs:** the result is recorded as legible, marginal or illegible. It is not a pass criterion, but an illegible 60-stud result is reported plainly.
+
+**If the simulator can't be run:** the result is **PHONE SIMULATOR NOT TESTED**, and Stage B stays blocked by gate 3.
+
+**Real phone:** NOT TESTED unless the owner runs it. Navigation feedback (gate 4) comes from the owner driving around the plaza ring and the highway route.
+
+## 5. Not in this plan
+- Building any sign.
+- Stages C and D.
+- Connector–highway join signs at (±100, −492).
+- Second signs.
+- Renaming.
+- Any gameplay change.
